# L §4.2 schedule(p, e, roll, cal): "the day of period p given by e (an int day of the month ...), moved by the roll
# code when it isn't a business day ... A day that doesn't exist in p (31 February) gives none".  2026-05-01 is a
# holiday (a Friday): following gives Monday 2026-05-04.  2026-05-31 is a Sunday: following would leave May, so
# modified_following goes back to Friday 2026-05-29; unadjusted keeps the day.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input len: calendar
input d1: int
input d31: int

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2025-12-01
  len = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], yearly [01-01, 01-06, 05-01, 05-03, 08-15, 11-01, 11-11, 12-25, 12-26])
  d1 = 1
  d31 = 31

ask q1: schedule(2026-05, d1, following, len), schedule(2026-05, d31, modified_following, len), schedule(2026-05, d31, unadjusted, len), schedule(2026-02, d31, following, len) law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: (2026-05-04, 2026-05-29, 2026-05-31, none)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
